# Member initialization and pointer names

Initialize every data member at its definition.

- Every member uses a `{}` initializer, including pointers.
- Pointer members use a `p` prefix.

```cpp
bool m_bOpen{};
SnaccWorkerPools* m_pWorkerPools{};
```

The `p` prefix is for every pointer, not only members. A member is `m_pWorkerPools`. A parameter or local is `pWorkerPools`.

Apply this to new and edited members. Do not rename unrelated existing members in the same change.
